{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7a42ae90aa3c488b455245ac132220b4efa83917b12e6d380d25d444603888f6","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review gate / LLM criteria routing","key_entities":["project.ci-gate-compat","criteria_routing.json","applies_to_globs","code_review.ci_config_globs","registry.project_applies_to_globs","gate_dispatch._activated_code_review_project_criteria","CodeReviewConfig","overlays/**/.github/workflows/**","**/Jenkinsfile*","**/.gitlab-ci.yml","**/.circleci/**","**/azure-pipelines*.y*ml","**/.buildkite/**","**/bitbucket-pipelines.yml","**/.drone.yml"],"problem_keywords":["code-review criterion","CI gate compatibility","hard-fail gates","in-flight branches","grandfather clause","portable design","project dogfood"],"propositions":["A newly added hard-fail CI gate or pipeline step can break in-flight branches created before the gate was introduced, causing regressions without a criterion to detect this incompatibility.","The code-review criterion dispatcher injects all activated project criteria unconditionally, regardless of whether their declared applies_to globs match the review's changed files.","Project-owned code-review criteria need to be gated by their applies_to glob patterns against the review's changed_files to enable selective activation only when relevant pipeline-config files are touched.","The applies_to glob set must be project-overridable via a config key so that unusual CI pipelines can be declared rather than enumerated in shipped code, supporting portability across CI vendors without vendor-specific code paths."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type